     * some basic bitmask concept
     * 
     * 
     * Set the ith bit: b(1<<i). Let i=0, so,
     * (1<<i) = 00001
     * 01010 | 00001 = 01011
     * 
     * Unset the ith bit: b & !(1<<i). Let i=1, so,
     * (1<<i) = 00010
     * !(1<<i) = 11101
     * 01010 & 11101 = 01000
     * 
     * Let i = 3
     * (1<<i) = 01000
     * 01010 & 01000 = 01000
     * 
     * Clearly the result is non-zero, so that means 3rd element is present in the
